a) When a customer arrives,
the simulation schedules the next arrival.
This keeps customers coming throughout the simulation.
For example, if customers arrive every 5 minutes,
an arrival at minute 10 schedules the next one for minute 15.


b) Starting service schedules a service completion event.
Its time is the start time plus the service duration.
For example, if service starts at minute "2" and takes 4 minutes,
it finishes at minute 6.
At that point, the customer leaves the single service point and the server becomes free.